<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roberto D'Aubuisson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–1992</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roberto D'Aubuisson was a Salvadoran army major and intelligence officer who founded the right-wing Nationalist Republican Alliance (ARENA) in 1981. He was linked to death squads during the civil war, and the UN Truth Commission found that he ordered the murder of Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscar-romero">Óscar Romero</a> in 1980. He presided over the Constituent Assembly in 1982–1983 and died of cancer in 1992.</p></div>
